error: `#[command]` needs a plain name for every argument: the name is the key the argument occupies in the invocation's `args`, and it is what a generated Dart or TypeScript client calls the parameter.
       A pattern, a `ref` binding or a `_` has no name to use.
       Fixes: bind a name and destructure in the body, or take the whole thing as one argument of a `#[derive(SharedState)]` struct.
